External dependencies and services
==================================

Command-line tools (all ship with a stock Omarchy install): curl, jq, sleep,
head (coreutils), sh.

Network services contacted over HTTPS (read-only GET/POST of public data;
no credentials required):
  - OSV.dev            https://api.osv.dev              (framework/library CVEs)
  - NVD API 2.0        https://services.nvd.nist.gov     (runtime/product CVEs)
  - CISA KEV feed      https://www.cisa.gov              (exploited-in-the-wild)
  - endoflife.date     https://endoflife.date            (EOL / latest patch)

An optional user-supplied NVD API key (stored in this plugin's own settings)
is sent only to services.nvd.nist.gov.

Privilege boundary: the plugin makes outbound HTTPS requests, opens advisory
URLs in the user's browser via xdg-open, and persists settings only to its own
entry in ~/.config/omarchy/shell.json. It does not modify any other user
configuration.
